is point in time so I figured I  would need quite a large dome on top of  the restaurants to kind of work against  the like the pretty large townhouses and  their heights that they have at the  moment so yeah that's what I wanted to  do with that and now this is actually  interestingly the only building where I  had 2 dormers but the government's don't  actually follow the rest of the layouts  of the building usually like every  single thing on the building follows the  same general layout so for instance the  the the little blocks on the balustrade  on top of the building are exactly in  the same line as the pillars of the  building which are at the same time  exactly in the same sort of vertical  line as the base of the walls of the  building and the same goes for the  windows usually I have the windows in  the exact same vertical line as the  Dorman's on top of the roof but this  building was actually one sort of  exception where I wanted to have 2  dormers just to see how it would kind of  work even though there are three windows  on every single floor I do kind of like  the effects but in general I'm just  slightly more of a fan of the more clean  looking having everything that  everything in the same vertical line  sort of approach to things now with that  out of the way and I just wanted to come  back to the restaurants again to do with  the townhouses having a little bit of a  better idea what the area around the  restaurants is going to look like and at  the tables and a bit of scenery around  the restaurants who make it look a  little bit more inviting I have got I  have gotten quite some comments about  the fact that the general park but  especially the Main Street doesn't look  very theme park ish there's the don't by  the way which is just very easily copied  over from another dome which I'll get to  later but I did get some comments about  the fact that the park isn't looking so  theme park ish because there aren't  really any signs or not too many signs  no no real theme park elements which is  still something that I'll add in the  main street as well some of it will be  added  screen but it also come back in some  future episodes as well but as you can  see here I'm also getting into some more  signs like for instance the like the ice  sort of you know what is that actually I  have no idea but like that neon thing  they're over there to kind of create a  bit more of an atmosphere and I'll get  into other type of restaurant signs and  things like that in the future as well  and when it comes to the dome it is just  a copy of the other dome out of pure  laziness and because it saves time and  it's a lot easier and it just felt like  the perfect dome in the way it looks and  also the size I just kind of placed it  and quickly took a look to see how well  it would actually work and if it kind of  offsets the heights of the town houses  around it pretty well and actually works  perfectly though just to make it a  little bit different and not the exact  same dome I did remove some of the  details and add a couple other things  and I did want to change the top a  little I wasn't too happy about the top  of the other dome there so I wanted to  try this more sort of cupola type thing  on top of the dome to have that little  dome on top of a dome kind of idea and  I'm actually really happy with how that  turned out and in general it is a bit  more of a fancy clean looking down than  the other one so you know that was the  general idea behind that building and  this is just about what I'll actually  get into this episode the rest of this  episode where I should be lighting or  something that I haven't really shown  off too much yet in the rest of the  series and also something which I didn't  get to quite a lot in the main street so  far so just something that I really  wanted to get to still though it's not  as interesting in terms of any decisions  that I had to make I just wanted to make  sure that everything was sort of more or  less well lit there are still some likes  lights are adjustments that I'll make in  the future because it is quite hard to  get this right sometimes many of the  lights like the lanterns are like have a  really small radius they don't really  spread out as much so they can be used  to create a general atmosphere but you  can't really use them to light anything  up and I find the only really good  things to light things up with the  spotlights but at some points there  wasn't really any  nearby where I could place a spotlight  without placing it in the middle of a  path so sometimes I was more or less  forced to use these little attach to  wall kind of lights but the sort of  drawback I find to the wall attached  lights is that they are really bright  and they really light up one particular  small part of the building a lot while  leaving the rest still somewhat dark one  general kind of thing I wanted to keep  in mind here though with the lighting is  that I wanted to have a more atmospheric  sort of feeling to all of the buildings  on the first floor so as you probably  saw all of the lights on the base floor  are just yellow lights and it's sort of  the lantern very orange lights and from  that point onward like the first and the  second floor and the third floor or have  these really white spotlights on them so  there is that contrast between having  the yellow base floor lit lights and the  the rest of the buildings where the  higher floors are all it is very white  light so yeah that was the general idea  there and for the rest I just wanted to  find a way to get this building to  actually light up because obviously this  is the biggest weenie in the park this  is actually the tallest building in the  entire park and I just wanted to make  sure that this building was quite lit  but I also didn't want it to be entirely  white like white really felt like a  color I didn't really want to have here  I wanted to have the tower be a little  bit more atmospheric than just at and  white it's just kind of harsh and not as  natural so I wanted to get this sort of  orangey yellow lights which lights up  the tower but at the same time is still  atmospheric and not too bright so I was  just kind of hard to get the exact right  spots because it's I just had to find  certain areas and certain buildings next  to this building certain places where I  could attach spotlights that would  actually work which is a bit of a hassle  at the moment in the future at least the  knee rotation of objects is going to  help out a lot and make things like this  a lot easier but at the moment you can't  really freely rotate what these  spotlights are going to be rotated  towards so it can be a bit of a  puzzle every now and then to get these  spotlights to be exactly where you want  them to be also I have to say I am like  no lighting master I know that to think  but yeah I am not that kind of person so  I just was kind of looking for a way to  get my buildings to look up to light up  in a nice way over here but in no way am  I like a real expert on this type of  thing unless you count my rct3  experience but that was a completely  different thing and not even that much  anyway and actually yeah over here at  the same sort of approach like the yeah  but the base floor is yellow over there  as well with the top floors being more  white but anyway yeah that's it for this  episode I am just about running out of  time lapse so thank you guys for  watching this episode in the next  episode I'll do some more work on the  Main Street mainly working on some new  townhouses and in the episode after that  which is just very newly recorded I'll  finish the main streets and maybe get to  something else so hope to see you then
 

